    <p class="eyebrow">ALEX BLYTHE · 2026-09-21 · RETAINED-EVIDENCE CORRECTION AUDIT</p>
    <h1>HX-CFD-QUAL-01 V2.1 acceptance-path correction</h1>
    <p class="lede">A bounded audit of the evaluator and retained fine-grid continuation evidence. No CFD was rerun, and the historical qualification disposition was not rescored.</p>
    <section class="verdict"><h2>Current disposition</h2><p class="status"><strong>DIAGNOSTIC_CORRECTION_COMPLETE</strong></p><p><strong>HX-CFD-QUAL-01 remains FAILED_NUMERICAL_GATES.</strong> Mesh independence remains NOT_EVALUATED. HX-03 and HX-04 remain blocked.</p></section>
    <section><h2>What was corrected</h2><ul><li>The field-stationarity predicate now requires non-empty finite normalized RMS updates at or below the frozen <code>0.001</code> limit. The prior predicate checked only that values were greater than zero.</li><li>The continuation analyzer now reports the retained <code>surfaceFieldValue</code> rows through 1000 s instead of claiming that post-800 s monitor rows were absent.</li></ul></section>
    <section><h2>Retained continuation evidence</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Result</th><th>Interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Shell outlet temperature span, 800–1000 s</th><td>0.002804 K</td><td>Supporting evidence; not a qualification pass</td></tr><tr><th>Tube outlet temperature span, 800–1000 s</th><td>0.001040 K</td><td>Supporting evidence; not a qualification pass</td></tr><tr><th>Tube U global normalized RMS, 900–1000 s</th><td>0.000762</td><td>Below the declared global stationarity limit for this interval</td></tr><tr><th>Tube U declared local normalized RMS</th><td>0.000791</td><td>Not a valid localized manifold metric; the mask covers 98.646% of tube cells</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
    <section><h2>Evidence limits that remain</h2><ul><li>The declared <code>x ≤ 0.05 m</code> mask contains 391,955 of 397,335 tube cells. It does not isolate the inlet manifold.</li><li>Field comparisons are positional/truncated rather than proven by explicit cell identity or topology correspondence.</li><li>Endpoint <code>p/p_rgh</code> values include negatives while the declared property-pressure interval begins at 0 Pa. Pressure-reference semantics remain <code>NOT_ESTABLISHED</code>.</li><li>Full hot/cold energy-storage closure and integrated conductive interface heat-rate evidence remain unresolved in this branch.</li></ul></section>
    <section><h2>Artifact integrity</h2><p>Continuation source immutability remains <strong>true</strong>. The corrected continuation manifest is parseable and verifies 219 artifacts with 0 missing and 0 mismatches.</p><p><a href="/demos/aero/hx-cfd-qual-01-acceptance-audit-2026-09-21/HX_CFD_QUAL_01_V2_1_ACCEPTANCE_AUDIT_REPORT.md">Download Markdown report</a> · <a href="/demos/aero/hx-cfd-qual-01-acceptance-audit-2026-09-21/HX_CFD_QUAL_01_V2_1_ACCEPTANCE_AUDIT_RESULTS.json">Download structured results</a> · <a href="/demos/aero/hx-cfd-qual-01-acceptance-audit-2026-09-21/SHA256_VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a></p></section>
    <section><h2>Next authorized step</h2><p>Repair the local-region definition, explicit field correspondence, pressure-reference interpretation, and complete energy/interface evidence in a versioned acceptance contract. Then decide whether a fresh three-grid campaign is warranted. No qualification or mesh comparison is authorized by this audit.</p></section>
    <p class="subtle">Prepared by Alex Blythe · Report date: <time datetime="2026-09-21">September 21, 2026</time>. This is an evidence correction, not a design release or experimental validation.</p>
